{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475494-why-not-use-twilight-rules","id":1475494,"title":"Why not use Twilight rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-26T08:16:14-08:00","id":1475494,"title":"Why not use Twilight rules?","content":"Both Helldiver's kith blessing and the Whispers of Morning contract transform the character into an incorporeal and invisible state. However, it is explicitly stated that it's not Twilight.<br /> I don't really understand why though.<br /> <br /> Interaction with other ephemeral entities is not the problem since the descriptions already state which Twilight frequencies the character can interact with.<br /> For instance, you could specify a &quot;Fae&quot; frequency shared by Hedge ghosts, incorporeal fae creatures and Whispers of Morning.<br /> Helldivers basically exist on all Twilight frequencies.<br /> <br /> Comparing it with Astral Projection from the Auspex Discipline I don't see why changeling powers couldn't do the same.<br /> <br /> Also: why there is no Twilight in the Hedge? Why the need to overcomplicate stuff, introducing a Dematerialized state for Hedge Ghosts that describes the same incorporeal state as Twilight but is not technically Twilight? Again, if the issue is interaction with other ephemeral stuff, wouldn't it be simpler to say that only beings with the &quot;Fae&quot; frequency can exist in Twilight within the Hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T08:51:38-08:00","id":1475495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475494-why-not-use-twilight-rules#post1475494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: why there is no Twilight in the Hedge? Why the need to overcomplicate stuff, introducing a Dematerialized state for Hedge Ghosts that describes the same incorporeal state as Twilight but is not technically Twilight? Again, if the issue is interaction with other ephemeral stuff, wouldn't it be simpler to say that only beings with the &quot;Fae&quot; frequency can exist in Twilight within the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no Twilight in the Hedge because there's never been Twilight in the Hedge since 1e, and because there's no Twilight <i>anywhere other than the material world</i>, for the most part. Mages creating Pocket Dimensions need to add the appropriate Subtle Arcanum for ephemeral beings to not be material within it; and while demons' Boltholes don't have &quot;No Twilight&quot; as an intrinsic quality a) boltholes are still attached to the material world, b) the quality can be added for the cheapest possible price, and c) demons are largely unique in having a primary antagonist type whose Twilight frequency they cannot perceive. Meanwhile, changelings occupy a metaphysic where abstractions can be bought as physical items at a market and dreams are a consistent otherworld that can physically harm you in the right circumstances.<br /> <br /> Also because, despite Hedge ghosts and hobgoblins both being disinclined to leave the Hedge for different reasons, they're both material in the Hedge and only one of them falls under the loosely-established category of &quot;things that can't (normally) materially leave the Hedge.&quot; Things that used to be nightmares and have neither acquired real flesh nor wholly retained their status as figments of the mind are nevertheless concrete threats in the borderland and much less so outside of it.<br /> <br /> The rules for Astral Projection make a vampire unable to interact with other ephemeral beings because Astral Projection is literally just projecting your senses around a place, whereas a Dematerialized Hedge ghost has a body and can use Numina and Influences as normal apart from the restriction on touch; the two are not equivalent.<br /> <br /> Also, even just from a descriptive perspective, &quot;fae Twilight&quot; doesn't look like Twilight. Hedge ghosts aren't occupying a phase of reality where &quot;physical objects appear pale and semi-translucent; light sources are dimmed, and sounds are distorted,&quot; and changelings doing the invisible-and-incorporeal thing have a natural source of Perception penalties to fill that niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-26T14:57:18-08:00","id":1475505,"title":"","content":"So basically, they\u2019re like the Strix. Non-ephemeral but still incorporeal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T02:40:45-08:00","id":1475828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475494-why-not-use-twilight-rules?p=1475495#post1475495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no Twilight in the Hedge because there's never been Twilight in the Hedge since 1e, and because there's no Twilight <i>anywhere other than the material world</i>, for the most part. Mages creating Pocket Dimensions need to add the appropriate Subtle Arcanum for ephemeral beings to not be material within it; and while demons' Boltholes don't have &quot;No Twilight&quot; as an intrinsic quality a) boltholes are still attached to the material world, b) the quality can be added for the cheapest possible price, and c) demons are largely unique in having a primary antagonist type whose Twilight frequency they cannot perceive. Meanwhile, changelings occupy a metaphysic where abstractions can be bought as physical items at a market and dreams are a consistent otherworld that can physically harm you in the right circumstances.<br /> <br /> Also because, despite Hedge ghosts and hobgoblins both being disinclined to leave the Hedge for different reasons, they're both material in the Hedge and only one of them falls under the loosely-established category of &quot;things that can't (normally) materially leave the Hedge.&quot; Things that used to be nightmares and have neither acquired real flesh nor wholly retained their status as figments of the mind are nevertheless concrete threats in the borderland and much less so outside of it.<br /> <br /> The rules for Astral Projection make a vampire unable to interact with other ephemeral beings because Astral Projection is literally just projecting your senses around a place, whereas a Dematerialized Hedge ghost has a body and can use Numina and Influences as normal apart from the restriction on touch; the two are not equivalent.<br /> <br /> Also, even just from a descriptive perspective, &quot;fae Twilight&quot; doesn't look like Twilight. Hedge ghosts aren't occupying a phase of reality where &quot;physical objects appear pale and semi-translucent; light sources are dimmed, and sounds are distorted,&quot; and changelings doing the invisible-and-incorporeal thing have a natural source of Perception penalties to fill that niche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, although personally I would like to see Twilight less of a specific metaphysical state or phenomenon in the CofD cosmology, and more like a general-purpose framework of rules that can be used for a broad spectrum of incorporeal and non-perceivable beings/powers, and that is used to describe and recreate a specific type of &quot;cinematic&quot; scenes.<br /> <br /> What I mean is that Twilight was designed specifically to recreate classic haunting scenes in CofD (since 1st ed). You're in an abandoned building and you feel a spooky presence even though it cannot be perceived through natural senses, it is incorporeal and intangible, etc. Classic. Some entity is in Twilight, everything works.<br /> On the other hand, Hedge Ghosts seem to have been made explicitly to bring haunting scenes in the Hedge. They even include examples of the Hedge equivalent of classic ghost stories. So you're in an abandoned Hollow and you feel a spooky presence even though it cannot be perceived through natural senses, it is incorporeal and intangible, etc. Is it Twilight? No, it's a Dematerialized Hedge Ghost.<br /> It's the same effect but not the same thing because... metaphysical reasons.<br /> <br /> The game is crunchy and complex enough as it is, so I feel it's a bit frustrating that a set of rules designed to describe, from a &quot;scene&quot; point of view, the same type of physical interaction and effect cannot be used because it's set in an otherworld so it needs its own set of rules to achieve the same result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T08:09:01-08:00","id":1475839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475494-why-not-use-twilight-rules?p=1475828#post1475828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, Hedge Ghosts seem to have been made explicitly to bring haunting scenes in the Hedge. They even include examples of the Hedge equivalent of classic ghost stories. So you're in an abandoned Hollow and you feel a spooky presence even though it cannot be perceived through natural senses, it is incorporeal and intangible, etc. Is it Twilight? No, it's a Dematerialized Hedge Ghost.<br /> It's the same effect but not the same thing because... metaphysical reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I want to be clear here, the &quot;haunting&quot; context of Hedge ghosts is that some Hedge ghosts form when people die in the Hedge \u2014 their default state is to be material beings unless they leave the Hedge, they don't tend to leave the Hedge for a number of reasons, and they can't Dematerialize inside the Hedge without spending Glamour.<br /> <br /> Hollow-haunts and the Lingering Dead are ghosts in the sense that they're remnants of dead people moreso than that they're numinous presences you can't see \u2014 they're phantom hitchhikers and inhospitable hosts that you later learn haven't been alive since the War of the Roses. The Hedge provides plenty of ways to lurk unseen that are less expensive than dissociating entirely from material interaction.<br /> <br /> All of which is to say nothing of the fact that the state of Twilight alone has never been the mechanical source for &quot;you feel a spooky presence even though it cannot be perceived through natural senses&quot; \u2014 that's the domain of supernatural powers and Merits like Unseen Sense or flaws in a particular being's makeup that allow it to be perceived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}